<h1>asymptotic bound</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A curve representing the limit of a function.  That is, the distance between a function and the curve tends to zero.  The function may or may not intersect the bounding curve.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bigOnotation.html"><em>asymptotic upper bound or O</em></a>, <a href="omega.html"><em>asymptotic lower bound or &omega;</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After Ben Podoll &lt;<a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="fa989f94909b979394d48a959e959696ba8f949ed494959e9b91d49f9e8f">[email&#160;protected]</a>&gt; 28 August 2003.</em>
</p>

